    {
      "entryId": "eph-2-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Salvation is gift, not wage — not of works. First principle: grace through faith excludes boasting at the root — the chain is God's mercy, faith's hand, God's gift; Jonah's fish-story agrees: salvation is of the LORD.",
      "density": 2.525,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Every named power in this age and the next is beneath the seated Christ. First principle: the ranking list is exhaustive — the name above every name outranks every throne the cosmic or political orders can produce.",
      "density": 2.2393,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-4-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Ascension implies a prior descent. First principle: the ascent to the throne required the descent to the lower earth — the psalm's logic holds the incarnation and the grave together.",
      "density": 2.1786,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-2-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The middle wall of partition is broken down. First principle: Christ does not make peace between Jew and Gentile — He is it; the dividing wall is demolished in His own body.",
      "density": 2.1714,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Election is in Christ and aims at holiness in love. First principle: the choice predates creation and its purpose is character — holy and blameless before Him, not merely selected by Him.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 8's footstool is given as headship over the body. First principle: the universe's subjection has a home address — the Head who fills all things exercises it first for the church.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Forgiveness according to the riches of His grace. First principle: redemption is present possession — the blood-price was paid once, and the forgiveness it bought is held, not hoped for.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-2-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Distance is overcome by blood, not by geography. First principle: the far-off Gentiles are brought near — Isaiah's peace to far and near is preached by the Peacemaker Himself.",
      "density": 1.925,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-4-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 4's evening rule for anger: felt, limited, sun-set. First principle: anger itself is permitted; its lodging overnight is not — do not give the devil a furnished room.",
      "density": 1.8679,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-5-31",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Genesis 2:24 quoted in the marriage section. First principle: marriage is the standing parable; the union of husband and wife preaches Christ and the church every day.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Genesis 2:24"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-6-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Helmet of salvation, sword of the Spirit. First principle: the Spirit's sword is the spoken Word — Isaiah's mouth-sword and Isaiah's helmet are handed to the believer.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-6-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The first armor piece is truth-girt loins, breastplate of righteousness. First principle: Isaiah 59's divine Warrior dresses; the church borrows His wardrobe — truth and righteousness as defensive gear.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-2-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus Himself being the chief corner stone. First principle: church structure is christologically centered, not merely institutional.",
      "density": 1.7964,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-2-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The exalted Christ preaches through the preachers — far and near in one sentence. First principle: Isaiah's messengers ran with peace; the Lord of the messengers delivers it Himself through them.",
      "density": 1.7464,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-5-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Walk in love as Christ gave Himself. First principle: the Levitical sweet-savour vocabulary is applied to the cross — self-giving love is the smell God loves.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-6-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The armor section opens with borrowed strength. First principle: Joel's beat-swords-into-armies call is inverted for the church — strength is received from the Lord, not mustered.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-5-32",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The mystery named: marriage was prophecy. First principle: Hosea's bridegroom God, Isaiah's Maker-Husband, and Genesis's one flesh all aimed here — Christ and His church.",
      "density": 1.7107,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-4-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 68's victory parade becomes the gift-dispensing ascension. First principle: the Conqueror shares the spoils — apostles, prophets, evangelists, pastors, teachers are the gifts He gave.",
      "density": 1.6786,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The fullness of times gathers heaven and earth into one Head. First principle: history has a unification plan — dispensational fullness, cosmic regathering, all things in Christ.",
      "density": 1.5893,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-5-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The presenting goal: holy, unblemished. First principle: the church's final form is ceremonial perfection — Psalm 45's bridal radiance granted, not grown.",
      "density": 1.5214,
      "words": 22,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-4-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Lying is put off because members belong to one another. First principle: Zechariah's true-speaking peace is communal — truth is the joint-fluid of the body.",
      "density": 1.4821,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-5-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Husbands love your wives as Christ loved the church and gave Himself for it. First principle: marriage is patterned on self-giving atonement, not mutual utility alone.",
      "density": 1.45,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "eph-1-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God raised Christ and seated Him at His right hand in heavenly places. First principle: resurrection is followed by enthronement above every name.",
      "density": 1.3179,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 13,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
